# MimOS package mirrors.
#
# Owned by mimos-release, so a mirror change ships as a package update rather
# than as an instruction to edit a file by hand.
#
# The primary mirror is enabled because it is published and answers.
# Verified on 2026-07-29 by fetching over HTTPS: signatures good against the
# key shipped in mimos-keyring, bytes identical to the locally built packages,
# and the database parses with nine entries.
#
# The rule that gated this has not changed: a configured repository that does
# not answer fails `pacman -Syu`, and the Live acceptance matrix runs exactly
# that. Never enable a mirror before confirming it answers.
# See packages/mimos-keyring/KEY.md.
#
# Signatures are required. The MimOS signing key travels in mimos-keyring,
# which is already in the image, so an installed system can verify this
# repository before it has ever contacted it.

